# DingTalk (钉钉)

Call DingTalk's new-gen OpenAPI via the bundled helper. **You are already
authenticated** — the egress proxy injects the enterprise access token on the
wire. Never ask for or handle tokens.

{{ACTION_AVAILABILITY_SECTION}}

## Usage

    python .opencode/skills/dingtalk/dingtalk_api.py <command> [args]

Output is JSON on stdout. A failure prints
`{"ok": false, "http_status": ..., "error": ...}` (or `errcode`/`errmsg`) —
surface the error message to the user. HTTP 403 with guidance means the action
needs approval (writes default to ASK); tell the user to approve it in Onyx.

List named routes with `routes`. Path placeholders (`{unionId}`, `{spaceId}`,
`{taskId}`, ...) are filled from `--data` fields; remaining GET fields become
query params, non-GET fields the JSON body.

```
dingtalk_api.py routes
dingtalk_api.py call <route> --data '<json>'
dingtalk_api.py raw GET /v1.0/<path> --data '<json>'   # escape hatch
```

### Knowledge base (钉钉文档 wiki)

Knowledge base calls need `operatorId` — the unionId of the acting user.

```
dingtalk_api.py call kb.list --data '{"operatorId":"<unionId>"}' --paginate
dingtalk_api.py call kb.nodes --data '{"operatorId":"<unionId>","parentNodeId":"<nodeId>"}' --paginate
dingtalk_api.py call kb.content --data '{"operatorId":"<unionId>","docKey":"<nodeId>","startIndex":0,"endIndex":199}'
```

List a workspace's tree by walking from its `rootNodeId`; node lists
return `nodes` plus a `nextToken` cursor. `kb.content` returns document
blocks (`result.data`, `blockType` + text payload) between the given
top-level indexes; page forward from the last `index` until an empty
page.

### Drive (钉盘)

```
dingtalk_api.py call drive.spaces --data '{"unionId":"..."}'
dingtalk_api.py call drive.files --data '{"spaceId":"...","unionId":"...","parentId":"0"}' --paginate
dingtalk_api.py call drive.download --data '{"spaceId":"...","fileId":"...","unionId":"..."}'
```

`drive.download` returns a pre-signed, time-limited CDN URL — fetch it
directly, without any auth header.

### Todo, calendar, contacts

```
dingtalk_api.py call todo.list --data '{"unionId":"..."}' --paginate
dingtalk_api.py call todo.create --data '{"unionId":"...","subject":"...","description":"..."}'
dingtalk_api.py call calendar.events --data '{"userId":"...","calendarId":"primary"}'
dingtalk_api.py call calendar.create --data '{"userId":"...","calendarId":"primary","title":"...","start":...,"end":...}'
dingtalk_api.py call contact.search --data '{"queryWord":"张三","offset":0,"size":10}'
dingtalk_api.py call contact.user --data '{"unionId":"..."}'
```

The enterprise token has no "me": for personal drive/todo/calendar data,
resolve the target person first — `contact.search` by name, then
`contact.user` to turn a `staffId` into a `unionId` — or ask the user.
Calendar APIs key on `userId` (staffId); drive/todo on `unionId`.

### Robot messages & AI cards

```
dingtalk_api.py call robot.o2o --data '{"robotCode":"...","userIds":["..."],"msgKey":"sampleText","msgParam":"{\"content\":\"hi\"}"}'
dingtalk_api.py call robot.group --data '{"robotCode":"...","openConversationId":"...","msgKey":"sampleMarkdown","msgParam":"{\"title\":\"...\",\"text\":\"...\"}"}'
```

`msgParam` is a JSON **string**, not a nested object. Sends default to ASK
approval — expect HTTP 403 while approval is pending, and tell the user to
approve it in Onyx. Deletes (todo/calendar) are denied.
